格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Search, pin and hide models in DeepSeek Harness; refresh provider catalogues.","id":"gh:1351186337","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-model-picker-augmented","slug":"ManoloRemiddi/dsh-model-picker-augmented","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","manolo-dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Search, pin and hide models in DeepSeek Harness; refresh provider catalogues."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-model-picker-augmented"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **MIT License** — Copyright (c) 2026 **Manolo Remiddi**\n> SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT — see LICEN"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"SE for the full license text."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Searchable, curated composer model picker for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This plugin replaces the model picker in the composer with a searchable version\nand adds a **Model P"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"icker Augmented** settings page so you can control exactly which\nmodels appear in the list and which"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" ones are pinned to the top."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Live model search** — a search field at the top of the model list filters\nas you type, matching "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"the model name **and** the provider name. Groups with\nno matches disappear; an empty query restores "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"the full list.\n- **Show / hide models** — hide models you never use from the picker list via\nthe set"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"tings page. Hidden models stay listed in Settings (marked *Hidden*)\nso you can bring them back whene"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ver you want.\n- **Pin to top** — pin your favorite models; they render in a *Pinned* section\nat the "},{"id":"p7s6","text":"very top of the model list (and are removed from their provider group\nbelow to avoid duplicates). Or"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"der them with the up/down arrows in Settings.\n- **Refresh providers** — this button first forces\nthe"},{"id":"p7s8","text":" running harness to re-read `~/.dsh/settings.yaml` from disk, so\nproviders and models you added to t"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"he file **appear without restarting the\nharness** — a new provider block in the file is served by th"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"e time the\nrefresh finishes. It then re-reads the live catalog and, for every active\nprovider that h"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"as a `baseURL`, checks the provider's endpoint and appends\nany models the file does not list yet to "},{"id":"p7s12","text":"the provider's `models` list in\n`settings.yaml` — a provider that has a `baseURL` but no `models` li"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"st yet\nfills itself in with a single click, no hand-editing. If the file sync\nitself fails, the refr"},{"id":"p7s14","text":"esh continues and reports it (`settings.yaml sync\nfailed: …`). The page also follows harness\ncatalog"},{"id":"p7s15","text":" changes pushed by the host (settings commits, adapter\nre-registrations, credential updates), so the"},{"id":"p7s16","text":" view stays live.\n- Keeps the rest of the picker exactly as shipped: the two-level Model/Effort\nmenu"},{"id":"p7s17","text":", effort levels, keyboard navigation, error/retry states, and full sync\nwith the `/model` command (b"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"oth use the same shared model directory)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) `>= 0.1.5-rc.1` (verified with 0.1.5-rc.1)\n- The web GUI profile (`--prof"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ile web`), which ships the dependencies this\nplugin builds on (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversat"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ion`,\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-model-selection`,\n`@deepsee"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"k-ai/dsh-client-locale`)."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Install the tested **1.1.2** package directly from its GitHub release:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Restart DSH and reload its web page. This package is distributed through\nGitHub Releases; it is not "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"published on npm. Existing users with a `link:`\ninstallation should update their linked checkout to "},{"id":"p13s3","text":"tag `v1.1.2` instead\nof adding a second copy. Keep your current settings and model credentials."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"For a source installation:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The plugin is a DSH bundle patch package (same pattern as other hot-pluggable\nweb plugins):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`pnpm install` matters: `link:` packages resolve their dependencies from their\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- The browser half registers into the composer's named model seat\n(`conversation.input.model`) with "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"a shadowing priority, and into the\nsettings panel (`settings.section`).\n- Model data comes from the "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"harness itself: the picker reads the same\nper-session advisory directory the shipped picker uses (th"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"e\n`modelDirectories` service), and the settings page fetches the global\ncatalog through the Remote A"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"PI (`remote.session.modelCatalog`). The plugin adds no\nmodel data of its own — if a model is missing"},{"id":"p19s6","text":" from the picker, it is missing\nfrom your configured provider catalogs (see below).\n- Curation (hidd"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"en models + pinned order) is **persisted durably on your\nmachine**: the node half registers a `model"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"-picker-augmented` settings\nnamespace, and every change is written through the harness settings syst"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"em\ninto `~/.dsh/settings.yaml` (`model-picker-augmented: { hidden: …,\npinned: … }`), so your pins an"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"d hidden models survive page refreshes,\nbrowser restarts, and machine restarts. On startup the brows"},{"id":"p19s11","text":"er half hydrates\nthe picker from that stored value.\n- **Refresh providers** (settings page) runs in "},{"id":"p19s12","text":"two stages, only when you click it:\n1. **Sync the harness with `settings.yaml`.** It issues a no-op "},{"id":"p19s13","text":"write\nthrough the settings commit API to the plugin's own\n`model-picker-augmented` namespace. Every "},{"id":"p19s14","text":"settings write forces the\nharness to re-read `settings.yaml` from disk before persisting, and any\nfi"},{"id":"p19s15","text":"le that has drifted — providers or models added by hand while the\nharness was running — is re-publis"},{"id":"p19s16","text":"hed through the normal settings\npipeline, so their routes are re-registered **live, without a restar"},{"id":"p19s17","text":"t**.\nOnly the plugin's curation section is rewritten; every other section of\nthe file passes through"},{"id":"p19s18","text":" untouched (comments included). If this step\nfails, the refresh continues with the in-memory catalog"},{"id":"p19s19","text":" and reports\n`settings.yaml sync failed: …`.\n2. **Re-read the catalog and sync the endpoints.** It t"},{"id":"p19s20","text":"hen fetches\n`remote.session.modelCatalog` (catalog + per-provider failures),\n`remote.llm.listProvide"},{"id":"p19s21","text":"rs` and `remote.llm.listConfigurableProviders`\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## DSH 0.1.5 compatibility (1.1.2)"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Version 1.1.1 used the removed `connection.api` browser interface and could\nstop the DSH GUI with “C"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"annot read properties of undefined (reading settings)”.\nVersion 1.1.2 declares the scoped `remote.se"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ttings`, `remote.llm`, and\n`remote.session` dependencies and uses their current methods, positional\n"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"arguments and Result values. Pins and hidden models retain their existing\nsettings namespace and for"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"ments and Result values. Pins and hidden models retain their existing\nsettings namespace and format."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Run `pnpm test` for regression coverage of client initialization, curation\nwrites, provider discover"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"y, revision-checked model additions and catalog\nerrors. Tests use an in-memory settings service and "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"never access credentials\nor live model endpoints."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Verified on 2026-09-10 with DSH 0.1.5-rc.1 and Chromium 152: the complete\nDSH GUI loads without plug"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"in failures, composer search filters models, the\nsettings catalog renders, and a pin survives a page"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" reload. The temporary\ntest pin was removed and the original curation settings were verified intact."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
